        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "406c71a3-c7e0-5a2c-8044-52e3f7e8c167",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Fighting Irish; Horrible Bosses; Hall Pass; We're the Millers; Horrible Bosses 2; Sleeping with Other People; Tumbledown; The Book of Love; Race\n- People: Dan Bakkedahl; Katrina Bowden; Henry Boyle; Anna Chlumsky; Siobhan Fallon Hogan; Chris Hoch; Alice Kremelberg; Nathan Lane; Boris McGiver; John F Mooney; Brian Murray; Maulik Pancholy; Lonny Ross; Molly Shannon; Jason Sudeikis; Kristen Sudeikis\n- Events: United States airing\n\nFacts:\n- The Fighting Irish aired in the United States on March 8, 2007.\n- The Fighting Irish featured guest appearances by Dan Bakkedahl, Katrina Bowden, Henry Boyle, Anna Chlumsky, Siobhan Fallon Hogan, Chris Hoch, Alice Kremelberg, Nathan Lane, Boris McGiver, John F Mooney, Brian Murray, Maulik Pancholy, Lonny Ross, Molly Shannon, Jason Sudeikis, and Kristen Sudeikis.\n- Jason Sudeikis starred in Horrible Bosses and Hall Pass in 2011.\n- Jason Sudeikis starred in We're the Millers in 2013 and Horrible Bosses 2 in 2014.\n- Jason Sudeikis starred in Sleeping with Other People and Tumbledown in 2015.\n- Jason Sudeikis starred in The Book of Love and Race in 2016.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ef659f4f-9061-5f6a-b9ff-e1f12e1b3924",
        "text": "Page: The Fighting Irish. Sentence: It aired on March 8, 2007 in the United States.\nPage: The Fighting Irish. Sentence: Guest stars who appeared in this episode were Dan Bakkedahl, Katrina Bowden, Henry Boyle, Anna Chlumsky, Siobhan Fallon Hogan, Chris Hoch, Alice Kremelberg, Nathan Lane, Boris McGiver, John F Mooney, Brian Murray, Maulik Pancholy, Lonny Ross, Molly Shannon, Jason Sudeikis and Kristen Sudeikis.\nPage: Jason Sudeikis. Sentence: He starred in the films \"Horrible Bosses\" (2011), \"Hall Pass\" (2011), \"We're the Millers\" (2013), \"Horrible Bosses 2\" (2014), \"Sleeping with Other People\" (2015), \"Tumbledown\" (2015), \"The Book of Love\" (2016) and \"Race\" (2016).",
